# Host paths for the "Inject" feature (docker-compose bind-mounts).
#
# Inject writes two files onto the host so the local Kiro IDE auto-logs-in as a
# pooled account:
#   - kiro-auth-token.json  -> the SSO token cache dir       (KIRO_HOST_CACHE_DIR)
#   - profile.json          -> the IDE extension globalStorage (KIRO_HOST_PROFILE_DIR)
#
# docker-compose.yml defaults both to their macOS locations. You only need this
# file if you run on Linux or Windows (or keep Kiro data in a non-default place).
# Copy it to .env and uncomment the block for your OS.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# NOTE: the profile dir path contains a space on macOS ("Application Support").
# Docker Compose interpolates these values as-is, so do NOT wrap them in quotes
# here — the quoting lives in docker-compose.yml.

# ── macOS (default — leave unset to use the compose defaults) ──────────────────
# KIRO_HOST_CACHE_DIR=${HOME}/.aws/sso/cache
# KIRO_HOST_PROFILE_DIR=${HOME}/Library/Application Support/Kiro/User/globalStorage/kiro.kiroagent

# ── Linux ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SSO cache is the same ~/.aws/sso/cache; globalStorage lives under XDG config
# (~/.config by default). If you set XDG_CONFIG_HOME, substitute it for ~/.config.
# KIRO_HOST_CACHE_DIR=${HOME}/.aws/sso/cache
# KIRO_HOST_PROFILE_DIR=${HOME}/.config/Kiro/User/globalStorage/kiro.kiroagent

# ── Windows ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use forward slashes; Docker Desktop accepts them. %APPDATA% is C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Roaming.
# KIRO_HOST_CACHE_DIR=C:/Users/<you>/.aws/sso/cache
# KIRO_HOST_PROFILE_DIR=C:/Users/<you>/AppData/Roaming/Kiro/User/globalStorage/kiro.kiroagent
